  <section class="pf-section" style="background:#f1f5f9;">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>What Happens During a Liverpool Power Flush?</h2>
      <p class="pf-sub">Step by step. Exactly what we do. No jargon. No surprises.</p>
      <div class="pf-steps">
        <div class="pf-step" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;"><div class="pf-step-num">1</div><div><strong>First check, 20 to 30 minutes</strong><p>We inspect the system. We check the boiler. We find the radiators with the worst blockages. We test a water sample to gauge the sludge level. We talk through any concerns with you before we start.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;"><div class="pf-step-num">2</div><div><strong>Cleaning chemical added and system run</strong><p>We add a pro-strength cleaner to the system. The heating runs for a while. That gives the cleaner time to loosen the sludge, magnetite and debris stuck to the inside of the pipes.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;"><div class="pf-step-num">3</div><div><strong>Flush machine hooked up</strong><p>We hook up the flush machine. The link point is at the boiler pump or a radiator tail. Which one depends on the system layout.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;"><div class="pf-step-num">4</div><div><strong>Full system flushed both ways, 60 to 90 minutes minimum</strong><p>The machine pumps water through the whole system in both directions. We reverse the flow over and over. That knocks the stubborn deposits loose. The dirty water flows through the machine's filter, which traps the debris.</p></div></div>
        <div class="pf-step" style="background:#ffffff;border:1px solid #e2e8f0;border-left:3px solid #f97316;border-radius:10px;padding:1rem 1.25rem;margin-bottom:0.75rem;"><div class="pf-step-num">5</div><div><strong>Each radiator flushed</strong><p>Each radiator is shut off and flushed one by one. The dirtiest ones may need an agitator tool to break up the worst deposits.</p></div></div>
        <div style="background:#1a3a5c;border-radius:8px;padding:1.25rem 1.5rem;margin-top:2rem;">
          <p style="color:#f97316;font-weight:800;font-size:0.88rem;margin:0 0 0.6rem;text-transform:uppercase;letter-spacing:0.05em;text-align:center;">Steps 6 to 9. Final Completion</p>
          <div style="display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:0.4rem;">
            <div style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);font-size:0.85rem;display:flex;gap:0.5rem;"><span style="color:#f97316;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">6.</span> Chemical neutraliser added. pH of system water checked to stop rust</div>
            <div style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);font-size:0.85rem;display:flex;gap:0.5rem;"><span style="color:#f97316;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">7.</span> System refilled with clean water and full-strength inhibitor to BS 7593 standard</div>
            <div style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);font-size:0.85rem;display:flex;gap:0.5rem;"><span style="color:#f97316;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">8.</span> System balanced. Working pressure set. Full heating and hot water cycle checked</div>
            <div style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.9);font-size:0.85rem;display:flex;gap:0.5rem;"><span style="color:#f97316;font-weight:700;flex-shrink:0;">9.</span> Written report given. It covers the date, sludge level, inhibitor added and final state. That's your boiler warranty proof.</div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
